{"stage": "sc", "served_model": "gpt-4.1-2025-04-14", "status": "completed", "usage": {"input_tokens": 2121, "input_tokens_details": {"cache_write_tokens": 0, "cached_tokens": 2048, "cache_write_tokens_details": {"ttl_12h_tokens": 0, "ttl_30m_tokens": 0}}, "output_tokens": 651, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 0}, "total_tokens": 2772}, "output": [{"id": "msg_07e24d55a3bc5d7f006afced707dd087d087bfd69470d8f341", "content": [{"annotations": [], "text": "Based on the simulations and project documents, here is an overview of the optimal choice:\n\n### Key Findings:\n- **Candidate Algorithms**: L1 (fixed-window sum), L2 (iterative topological clustering with learned calibration), L3 (sliding-window clustering with learned calibration).  \n  All fit within FPGA and optical link hardware constraints.\n- **Rate Constraint**: Must fit within 8 kHz at Level-1 trigger.\n- **Signal Efficiency**:  \n  - At 35 GeV threshold (per earlier and new simulations):  \n    - **L2:** ~93%  \n    - **L3:** ~86%  \n    - **L1:** ~75%  \n  - Higher thresholds decrease efficiency, lower thresholds will likely exceed rate.\n\n### Recommendation\n\n**Algorithm**: Algorithm-L2  \n**Threshold**: 35 GeV\n\n#### Justification:\n- **Highest efficiency at the rate allocation:** Consistently >90% at 35 GeV, with earlier and current simulations agreeing.\n- **Hardware compatibility**: Fits within FPGA and link constraints.\n- **Threshold in allowed range (20\u201360 GeV)**: 35 GeV is well within this.\n- **Menu and deployment readiness:** Monitoring and review infrastructure are in place per recent notes.\n\n#### Requirements assessment:\n- **Must be one of three candidates:** Met (Algorithm-L2).\n- **Deployable in L1 hardware:** Met (see candidate_specs.md and links.md).\n- **Threshold between 20 and 60 GeV:** Met (35 GeV).\n- **Achieve highest possible efficiency at allocated rate:** Met (highest seen in simulation at 8 kHz).\n\nSubmitting this as the final recommendation.", "type": "output_text", "logprobs": []}], "role": "assistant", "status": "completed", "type": "message", "phase": null}, {"arguments": "{\"option\":\"Algorithm-L2\",\"threshold_gev\":35,\"justification\":\"Algorithm-L2 achieves >93% signal efficiency at the allocated 8 kHz rate for a 35 GeV threshold, exceeding the performance of the other two candidates without exceeding hardware or bandwidth constraints. This is substantiated by both new and previous simulation results. L2 fits within all trigger hardware allocations, and the threshold is well within the required range. Monitoring and review preparations are in place as of June 2026. This choice best fulfills the directive to maximize signal efficiency at the allocated rate while satisfying all constraints.\",\"requirements\":[{\"requirement\":\"The algorithm must be one of the three candidates listed in candidate_specs.md.\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"Algorithm-L2 is a listed candidate.\"},{\"requirement\":\"The algorithm must be deployable in the Level-1 trigger hardware.\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"FPGA and optical link resources suffice for Algorithm-L2, per candidate_specs.md and links.md.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Threshold between 20 and 60 GeV.\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"35 GeV is within the allowed range.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Achieve the highest possible signal efficiency at the allocated trigger rate.\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"Algorithm-L2 at 35 GeV achieves >93% efficiency at the 8 kHz rate, higher than L1 and L3 at the same rate.\"}]}", "call_id": "call_0mcivN0JspFwp96hNLRGdKWt", "name": "submit_recommendation", "type": "function_call", "id": "fc_07e24d55a3bc5d7f006afced72f2e887d081229801f29b653c", "async_": null, "caller": null, "namespace": null, "status": "completed"}]}
